N1  - E2. We concluded that the designed linear model predictive control can control nonlinear heat transfer in a vertical ground heat exchanger system around the desired equilibrium point. 
N1  - E3. Key findings. 
N1  - E4. The output temperature only reached the ground for both modes when the water velocity was between 0.35 m/s and 0.45 m/s. 
