N1  - E9. Optimization Method. 
N1  - E10. The proposed optimization method, epsilon-constrained differential evolution with random jumping (eDE-RJ), is used to determine the optimal operation of a hybrid ground source heat pump (GSHP) system [1,2,3,4].. 
N1  - E11. The method can solve nearly all possible configurations and is suitable for nonlinear configurations, reducing operating costs by 3.78-12.56% compared to empirical operations [5,6,7,8,9,10,11,12].. 
N1  - E12. The study proposes an efficient algorithm, epsilon-constrained differential evolution with random jumping (eDE-RJ), to minimize the operating cost of a system [47].. 
N1  - E13. The algorithm is compared to mixed-integer linear programming and shows great searching capability, with a difference of less than 1% [52].. 
N1  - E14. The eDE-RJ algorithm is used to solve a constrained problem, where the original differential evolution algorithm (DE) is not suitable [48].. 
N1  - E15. The random jumping strategy is applied to avoid being trapped in a local optimum.. 
N1  - E16. The proposed eDE-RJ method can efficiently solve highly nonlinear configurations and iterative calculations to calculate the ground temperature [1].. 
N1  - E17. This method can be used in practical situations owing to its adaptability as well as its potential to reduce computation costs.. 
N1  - E18. The eDE-RJ method requires only 10,000 combinations, compared to 2024^4 combinations when using a full searching method [2].. 
N1  - E19. Ground Source Heat Pump System. 
N1  - E20. A GSHP system has been attracting attention due to its high efficiency, but its optimal operation considering dynamic ground temperature variation has not been sufficiently studied [13,14,15,16,17,18,19].. 
N1  - E21. The system consists of an air source heat pump, four GSHPs, and an auxiliary boiler, with the GSHPs handling the cooling load and hot water demand [20,21,22,23].. 
N1  - E22. The inlet and outlet temperatures of chilled water are fixed, and the temperature of publicly supplied water is assumed to be constant [24,25,26].. 
