N1  - E35. The average fluid temperature of the BHE, Tf , is usually approximated by the arithmetic mean of the inlet and outlet temperatures.. 
N1  - E36. Simulation And Calculation. 
N1  - E37. The calculation steps for the GSHP performance are as follows: (1) In the first time step t0, the GSHP’s inlet fluid temperature is the same as the initial ground temperature, Tf ;outðt0Þ 1⁄4 THP;inðt0Þ 1⁄4 T0 [27]. (2) Using the heat exchange rate of the previous time step, Q bheðtkÀ1Þ, the current time step’s borefield temperature, Tbf ðtkÞ, is calculated using Eqs. (2)–(4), and Tf ðtkÞ is also calculated using Eq (17).. 
N1  - E38. A virtual hotel building in Tokyo with a total floor space of 1000 m2 was considered, with cooling and hot water loads for 24 h calculated at time steps of 1 h, and a dynamic electricity price with time was assumed, based on Ref. [45] [46].. 
N1  - E39. System Operation. 
N1  - E40. The system operation is optimized using the eDE-RJ algorithm, with the aim of minimizing the operating cost [47].. 
N1  - E41. The system consists of multiple machines, including air-source heat pumps (ASHP), ground-source heat pumps (GSHP), and absorption chillers (AB).. 
N1  - E42. The optimization is conducted for different cases, including Case 1, which has a calculation period of 24 hours, and Case 2, which has a calculation period of 7 days [49, 50].. 
N1  - E43. The results show that the optimal operation schedule and heat generation of the machines can be determined using the eDE-RJ algorithm.. 
N1  - E44. Case Studies. 
N1  - E45. The study conducts two case studies, Case 1 and Case 2, to confirm the effectiveness of the proposed optimization method [51].. 
N1  - E46. In Case 1, the calculation period is 24 hours, and the optimization is conducted for three different scenarios: Case 1-1, where the GSHPs' operation is set as the first priority; Case 1-2, where the eDE-RJ algorithm determines the start and stop times of operation; and Case 1-3, where the eDE-RJ algorithm determines the amount of heat generation of all machines at each time step.. 
N1  - E47. The results show that the operating cost can be reduced by 5.27% and 9.09% in Case 1-2 and Case 1-3, respectively, compared to Case 1-1 [47].. 
N1  - E48. Operating Costs. 
N1  - E49. The operating costs of Cases 2-2 and 2-3 were reduced by 1.15% and 2.20% compared to Case 2-1, respectively [3].. 
N1  - E50. The simplified optimization strategy could reduce the operating costs compared to the empirical operation for a single day and 7 days by 3.78% and 9.59%, respectively [4].. 
N1  - E51. Ground Temperature. 
N1  - E52. The thermal history exchanged between the ground and the GSHP has a long-lasting effect due to the large thermal capacity of the ground [6].. 
N1  - E53. The performance of GSHPh was gradually degraded compared to its initial condition because of the thermal depletion of the ground [7].. 
